    "body": "> tree walkers are used in **a fifth of all pages**, exactly because manual traversal of every single node on the page tends to be inefficient\n\nExcept most of those usage happens in third party content and the actual usage in first-party resources is 0.58% to 1.63%. That's an order of magnitude smaller.\n\nWhat are concrete use cases for `NodeIterator` or `TreeWalker` to cross shadow boundaries?",
